### 4.3 Forbidden Code Patterns

The following patterns are prohibited and enforced by ESLint at `error` severity:

```typescript
// PROHIBITED — eval
eval('doSomething()');

// PROHIBITED — new Function (equivalent to eval)
const fn = new Function('return 1 + 1');

// PROHIBITED — string form of setTimeout/setInterval
setTimeout('console.log("hello")', 100);
setInterval('processQueue()', 1000);

// PROHIBITED — exec with string interpolation from user data
import { exec } from 'child_process';
exec(`ls ${userInput}`);

// PROHIBITED — any type annotation
function process(data: any): any { ... }

// PROHIBITED — non-literal RegExp with user input (ReDoS)
const re = new RegExp(userInput);
```

